      "locked": false,
      "text": "Module 4: SQL\n\n-> SQL treats relations as a \"MULTISET or BAG\". Which is different from relational algebra and relational calculus.\n-> There are no NULL values in Relational Algebra and Relational Calculus. SQL have them. Outer Join is not considered a part of relational algebra and calculus.\n-> Relations in SQL may not have a candidate key.\n-> If a relation in SQL has a key, Then there wouldn't be any duplicate rows.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Module 4: SQL\n\n-> SQL treats relations as a \"MULTISET or BAG\". Which is different from relational algebra and relational calculus.\n-> There are no NULL values in Relational Algebra and Relational Calculus. SQL have them. Outer Join is not considered a part of relational algebra and calculus.\n-> Relations in SQL may not have a candidate key.\n-> If a relation in SQL has a key, Then there wouldn't be any duplicate rows.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
