      "text": "Active Recall  -  C Programming & Data Structures\n\n-> Storing higher word size integer in lower and vice versa\n-> Interpretation of above kind of operations and Will this happen at any other places?\n\n-> Implicit conversion of primitive data types while evaluating an expression.\n\n-> Switch statement strucute. Rules for exp, case labels, default, break.\n-> What is \"Fall-through\"?\n\n-> Right shift Operator and rules for unsigned and signed and undefined behavior scenarios\n-> Left shift Operator and rules for unsigned and signed and undefined behavior scenarios\n\n-> What is a sequence point and list all.\n\n-> Operator Precedence table\n\n-> Function declaration and definition syntax. And a quirk about return type in function declaration.\n\n-> Memory Layout\n\n-> Storage Classes and their (scope, lifetime, linkage, default value, location)",
